---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { readBuildIntent } from "../site/build-intent";

readBuildIntent();
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Mythic China handles personal information in the current review state and planned reader services."
>
  <article class="privacy-page page-shell" data-review-notice="privacy">
    <header class="privacy-hero section-space">
      <p class="section-context">Privacy Notice</p>
      <h1>Clear boundaries for reader information.</h1>
      <p>
        This notice distinguishes what is available now from services that are
        still planned and inactive.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-09-02">September 2, 2026</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content section-space">
      <section id="controller" aria-labelledby="controller-heading">
        <h2 id="controller-heading">Controller and contact</h2>
        <p>
          Mythic China is a site brand operated by hyc. For this notice, hyc is
          the named data controller and is based in China.
        </p>
        <address>
          Privacy and data-rights contact:
          <span class="privacy-address">huyichen2019@gmail.com</span>
        </address>
        <p>
          Use the subject “Privacy request” for access, correction, deletion, or
          complaint requests. The address is plain text and does not create an
          automatic email action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="current-state" aria-labelledby="current-state-heading">
        <h2 id="current-state-heading">Current review state</h2>
        <p>
          This noindex review is not currently accepting newsletter sign-ups and
          is not currently accepting Reader Requests. Its disabled controls do
          not send or store information.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only current contact route described here is a message that you
          independently choose to send to the public Gmail address above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact-data" aria-labelledby="contact-data-heading">
        <h2 id="contact-data-heading">Privacy-request correspondence</h2>
        <p>
          A message may include your email address, its contents, attachments
          you choose to send, and delivery metadata. We use it only to handle
          and document your request.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google provides the Gmail mailbox. Our operating rule is to retain the
          correspondence for 60 days after a request is closed, then delete it
          from the active mailbox and Trash, unless a longer retention period is
          required by law. Google’s underlying deletion and backup processes
          follow its own retention terms and may take longer; 60 days is not a
          supplier-level hard-deletion guarantee.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="newsletter" aria-labelledby="newsletter-heading">
        <h2 id="newsletter-heading">Planned Newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          If activated after separate account verification, the Newsletter will
          use Buttondown to process an email address for new stories and
          occasional editorial selections, no more than twice a month.
          Subscription will require email confirmation, every message will
          include an unsubscribe route, and open and click tracking will remain
          off before the first send and afterward.
        </p>
        <p>
          Buttondown is a United States provider, and its planned service domain
          is buttondown.com. No Buttondown account, exact action, subscriber
          record, or verified deletion workflow is active in this review. This
          notice will be updated before sign-ups open.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="reader-request" aria-labelledby="reader-request-heading">
        <h2 id="reader-request-heading">Planned Reader Request</h2>
        <p>
          If activated after separate form verification, the hosted Tally form
          will process the Entry page ID and required topic suggestion. An email
          address will be optional and will require separate consent used only
          to follow up about that suggestion; it will not subscribe the reader
          to the Newsletter.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tally creates a persistent Respondent ID in browser localStorage and
          may reuse it across forms in the same Tally workspace. That provider
          identifier will not become a Mythic China content ID, analytics
          property, or internal grouping key. Submission email notifications
          will remain off.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tally is a Belgian provider whose planned service domain is tally.so;
          its documentation states that form data is stored in Google Cloud
          Belgium. No exact hosted-form link or account is active here. Deleting
          submissions and Trash does not remove a Respondent ID already stored
          in a visitor’s browser; the account-level behavior and exit path must
          be verified before activation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The planned low-cost operating rule is to review submissions every 28
          days, delete records that are at least 60 days old, and empty Tally
          Trash in the same operation. When performed on time, this produces an
          expected retention window of about 60 to 88 days. The sole operator is
          hyc, with no independent backup; a missed operation can extend that
          period. Tally is not active in this review.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="analytics-hosting" aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
        <h2 id="analytics-heading">Analytics and hosting</h2>
        <p>
          Plausible is not enabled. This review contains no analytics script,
          event producer, cookie banner, or remote analytics request. If later
          approved, the planned provider is Plausible at plausible.io; exact
          script and request domains must be verified before activation.
        </p>
        <p>
          No Vercel project or production origin is configured. A stable Vercel
          production hostname may be adopted during a separately authorized
          public-release stage, while generated preview and commit URLs will not
          be used as canonical URLs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights" aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
        <h2 id="rights-heading">Your choices and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          Contact the address above to ask what personal information we hold, to
          request correction or deletion, to withdraw an optional follow-up
          consent, or to raise a privacy complaint. We may ask for only the
          information needed to verify and complete the request.
        </p>
        <p>
          This notice will be revised before any planned provider becomes active
          and again if the site adopts a custom domain or a different processor.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
